{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01568",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 1.2,
      "end_seconds": 6.89,
      "duration_seconds": 5.69,
      "text": "All set here, doctor. Chart's updated, and I'll read the readings out when you're ready."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 8.05,
      "end_seconds": 11.94,
      "duration_seconds": 3.89,
      "text": "Okay, thanks. Hi, how can I help today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 13.99,
      "end_seconds": 19.94,
      "duration_seconds": 5.95,
      "text": "Hello, doctor. I'm here with them in case I can help."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 21.73,
      "end_seconds": 26.09,
      "duration_seconds": 4.36,
      "text": "Of course, please stay. It's helpful to have you here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 26.66,
      "end_seconds": 40.07,
      "duration_seconds": 13.41,
      "text": "It's a very sore throat. I thought I'd wait, but it hasn't gone. I told myself I'd wait and see, and here I am."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 44.73,
      "end_seconds": 48.36,
      "duration_seconds": 3.63,
      "text": "Can you tell me when it first started?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 51.44,
      "end_seconds": 53.71,
      "duration_seconds": 2.27,
      "text": "Probably ten days. Yeah."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 55.28,
      "end_seconds": 62.98,
      "duration_seconds": 7.7,
      "text": "Can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 66.04,
      "end_seconds": 73.8,
      "duration_seconds": 7.76,
      "text": "Swallowing definitely sets it off. Mostly moderate. There's swollen glands in my neck as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 75.41,
      "end_seconds": 78.5,
      "duration_seconds": 3.09,
      "text": "Is it bearing on you a lot?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 79.82,
      "end_seconds": 100.27,
      "duration_seconds": 20.45,
      "text": "Mostly mild. I've been feeling exhausted too, for two days. With feeling exhausted, mostly mild. As for fever, I honestly can't say when that began. It might have been last month or the month before."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 102.29,
      "end_seconds": 104.46,
      "duration_seconds": 2.17,
      "text": "Tell me your medicines, please."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 105.25,
      "end_seconds": 113.42,
      "duration_seconds": 8.17,
      "text": "Simvastatin, 20 milligrams, at night. Alendronate. I take it 70 milligrams, once a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 114.73,
      "end_seconds": 119.32,
      "duration_seconds": 4.59,
      "text": "Doctor, our chart from the last visit lists it as 35 milligrams."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 119.85,
      "end_seconds": 125.37,
      "duration_seconds": 5.52,
      "text": "Okay. Have you got the newest prescription or the box with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 126.25,
      "end_seconds": 138.28,
      "duration_seconds": 12.03,
      "text": "I don't think I have it with me. I'm on throat lozenges, when needed. Sorry, I know I'm rambling a bit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 148.98,
      "end_seconds": 153.03,
      "duration_seconds": 4.05,
      "text": "Are there any allergies I should be aware of?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 153.57,
      "end_seconds": 157.9,
      "duration_seconds": 4.33,
      "text": "Oh, no, I've never reacted to anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 161.35,
      "end_seconds": 168.46,
      "duration_seconds": 7.11,
      "text": "Hold on, doctor, I think she reacted to erythromycin once. I'm not certain, though."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 169.68,
      "end_seconds": 174.44,
      "duration_seconds": 4.76,
      "text": "Erm, you know, really? I don't think so."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 175.86,
      "end_seconds": 180.77,
      "duration_seconds": 4.91,
      "text": "Fair enough, I'll write down both versions. Alright, how about smoking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 181.55,
      "end_seconds": 185.23,
      "duration_seconds": 3.68,
      "text": "I gave up cigarettes last spring."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 186.49,
      "end_seconds": 188.44,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "And alcohol, how much?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 189.08,
      "end_seconds": 194.49,
      "duration_seconds": 5.41,
      "text": "I used to drink heavily but I stopped four years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 195.64,
      "end_seconds": 197.71,
      "duration_seconds": 2.07,
      "text": "Do you get out much?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 199.35,
      "end_seconds": 204.28,
      "duration_seconds": 4.93,
      "text": "Not much, I mostly stay in these days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 205.41,
      "end_seconds": 209.59,
      "duration_seconds": 4.18,
      "text": "What does a normal day of food look like?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 210.56,
      "end_seconds": 214.15,
      "duration_seconds": 3.59,
      "text": "Lots of rice, lentils and some fruit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 217.84,
      "end_seconds": 219.54,
      "duration_seconds": 1.7,
      "text": "Who lives with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 220.59,
      "end_seconds": 223.06,
      "duration_seconds": 2.47,
      "text": "My partner and our baby."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 224.92,
      "end_seconds": 227.35,
      "duration_seconds": 2.43,
      "text": "What about your medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 229.21,
      "end_seconds": 241.34,
      "duration_seconds": 12.13,
      "text": "Yes, heart failure. I took the morning off to come in today. High cholesterol, for about a year. I've got thin bones."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 242.03,
      "end_seconds": 242.93,
      "duration_seconds": 0.9,
      "text": "Anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 244.64,
      "end_seconds": 246.59,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "Has there been any jaundice?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 247.24,
      "end_seconds": 248.94,
      "duration_seconds": 1.7,
      "text": "Nope, no jaundice."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 249.53,
      "end_seconds": 256.88,
      "duration_seconds": 7.35,
      "text": "Okay, go on. Did you get difficulty breathing, tummy pain on the left or rash?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 261.76,
      "end_seconds": 265.46,
      "duration_seconds": 3.7,
      "text": "No, I haven't had any of them."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 266.25,
      "end_seconds": 268.85,
      "duration_seconds": 2.6,
      "text": "Any breathing difficulties apart from this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 270.26,
      "end_seconds": 271.85,
      "duration_seconds": 1.59,
      "text": "No, nothing there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 273.41,
      "end_seconds": 282.31,
      "duration_seconds": 8.9,
      "text": "Doctor, I've got the readings for you. Temperature 38.3, heart rate 97, oxygen saturation is 98 percent, pressure 115 over 71."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 282.99,
      "end_seconds": 284.01,
      "duration_seconds": 1.02,
      "text": "Okay, noted."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 286.37,
      "end_seconds": 290.95,
      "duration_seconds": 4.58,
      "text": "I'd like to check you over now, if that's alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 308.49,
      "end_seconds": 309.19,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 310.96,
      "end_seconds": 312.28,
      "duration_seconds": 1.32,
      "text": "Look straight ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 323.37,
      "end_seconds": 330.44,
      "duration_seconds": 7.07,
      "text": "Your tonsils are large with white coating and the glands in the neck are tender."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 335.71,
      "end_seconds": 352.25,
      "duration_seconds": 16.54,
      "text": "All finished, thank you. So, based on the history and the examination, my working impression is glandular fever. I want to be honest that this is an impression, not a final answer. Streptococcal tonsillitis is still possible."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 353.73,
      "end_seconds": 357.36,
      "duration_seconds": 3.63,
      "text": "Is this serious, you know, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 358.87,
      "end_seconds": 366.82,
      "duration_seconds": 7.95,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like glandular fever, but I'd like to confirm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 383.55,
      "end_seconds": 412.5,
      "duration_seconds": 28.95,
      "text": "I'll request a monospot test, it'll help with sore throat and fatigue. The result will help us decide whether anything more is needed. Let's book a blood count to look into glandular fever. Rest, plenty of fluids, and no contact sport for a month because of the spleen. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 413.26,
      "end_seconds": 415.74,
      "duration_seconds": 2.48,
      "text": "Thank you, that's clear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 416.78,
      "end_seconds": 428.88,
      "duration_seconds": 12.1,
      "text": "Come back or go to emergency straight away if the symptoms get worse. Let's plan a check in two weeks. That's everything on my side. Anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 429.72,
      "end_seconds": 434.06,
      "duration_seconds": 4.34,
      "text": "Oh, okay, that makes sense. Thanks for explaining."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 434.76,
      "end_seconds": 436.8,
      "duration_seconds": 2.04,
      "text": "Okay, goodbye for now."
    }
  ]
}